junkies jace perhaps naively  believes he can broker a peace deal with  silko but each side demands something  neither is likely to give up for example  jace wants jinx handed over to him jinx  was responsible for several attacks over  the course of episodes 4 to 9 including  an attack which left several enforcers  including sheriff marcus dead as we  learned later on in the episode silco  never had any intention of turning jinx  over for him it would be like turning  over his own daughter i never would have  given you to them  not for anything the same can be said  for silco's demands he wanted free trade  routes blanket amnesty access to the hex  gates and most importantly sovereignty  this would establish the nation of zan  something he fought for his entire life  he could have had that nation but his  love for jinx was stronger but before we  get more into that silco has to deal  with a coup within his criminal  organization finn believes silko is weak  the undercity has grown chaotic under  his rule and it's time for a change he  even has another member on his side  rennie who was the mother of the boy  jace killed silco gives a speech about  loyalty how that was the only thing that  got him and the others through the dark  days of the past and as it looks like  silko's days are numbered cevica ends up  killing finn perhaps out of loyalty  civica will later fight vai where she  gets her arm ripped off and thrown into  the jukebox the same jukebox player that  starts every episode but what i really  want to discuss is the last shot we see  of her she's in silko's office lighting  her cigar with finn's lighter silko's  chair is empty in the background  suggesting she will be the one to take  over with silko dead at the end of the  episode the underground doesn't have a  leader and she just might be the one to  step up victor is reeling from the death  of sky the two had a high school-like  romance over the course of the season  and she ended up disintegrating when  trying to help victor release himself  from the now corrupted hex core victor's  experiments let him down a dangerous  path where he ended up taking shimmer  and combining it with hextech to prolong  his life it's kind of ironic since his  mentor singe did similar nefarious  experiments in order to prolong the life  of his pet rio in both instances someone  they loved was killed victor is so  overcome with grief and the decisions  that he's made over the season that he  even contemplates suicide before jace  interrupts him skye's letter to him  talked about how he's made the world a  better place but for him he thinks he's  just made it worse he even tries to  break the corrupted hextech but is  unable to but we're not exactly sure if  this is because he's linked to it or  just doesn't have the courage the last  two episodes also see the introduction  of embessa medarda who appears to be a  prominent member of the noxus empire one  of league of legends many factions and  bessa sent her daughter mel to piltover  because she thought she lacked spine  embezza also says of mel you weakened me  i couldn't endure the look in your eyes  whenever i made the decisions the  necessary decisions to keep us safe in  ambassador's mind a ruler must be quote  a fox and a wolf both cunning and strong  and melt certainly is cunning but as we  see in episode 8's intro she lacks the  cutthroat nature her mother is looking  for mel paints a large mural of the  immortal bastion fortress surrounded by  noxus ships furthering her connection  with the empire but in one of the  season's final scenes we see she's  ruined it symbolic of her turning her  back on her mother and the empire we  also get word that mel's brother has  died but it's never mentioned who he  could be this is likely jay madarda a  playable card from the legends of  roonterra and heir apparent to the  medarda fortune jace tells victor that  they must destroy the hexcore its power  if in the wrong hands could cause  absolute devastation the potential for  this technology to be used against them  is something heimerdinger warned them of  several times heimerdinger is several  hundred years old and can recall times  in which magic nearly destroyed the  world no one heeds heimerdinger's  warnings and he's eventually kicked off  the council teaming up with a now  grown-up echo in his team of rebels  known as the firelights this  heimerdinger echo combo may be the  biggest clue as to what happens in the  wake of jinx's rocket attack but i'll  get to that in a bit silko drinks his  sorrows beneath a statue of vander a man  who was like a brother to him they both  wanted the same thing to see a world  where the people of zan could live free  just like the people topside but they  differed in how to achieve this silco  believed violence was the answer and  vander did not this  it's not gonna solve your problems  it just makes more of them it culminated  in the two duking it out with silko  almost drowning to death now silko  drinks alone living with the fact his  dream of an independent zone is right in  front of him but knowing he can't do  what it takes to achieve it that is give  up jinx after vander gave up life to  protect vi and powder jinx's name as a  child silko took in jinx and raised her  as his own since then jinx has done  silko's bidding but leaving her sister  vai abandoned her but later in the  series jinx overhears what really  happened those many years ago and  struggles with who is telling the truth  does she believe her sister or the man  who raised her but it seems jinx is too  far gone she's haunted by the voices of  her past pushing her in different  directions and silco fearing vaya's  swing jinx into madness grabs a nearby  pistol and aims now this is up to  interpretation but i believe he was  pointing the gun at vi to get her to  stop talking and jinx overcome by the  instinct to protect her sister shoots  silco in the process it's a terribly  tragic ending i should also mention  before we continue that caitlyn is also  here she gets knocked out by jinx but  it's been subtly hinted that vi and  caitlyn might eventually end up together  i thought i'd bring it up because i know  someone in the comments definitely will  in the lore the two eventually do become  partners in law enforcement so it's  definitely possible in the season's  final moments we get a montage of  various characters which lead up to  jinx's rocket attack and there's a ton  of cool stuff to unpack here that may  give us clues for season 2. the first is  jinx's decision to sit in the chair  marked jinx confirming her complete  transformation from powder to jinx there  was another chair that said powder yet  she chose to sit in this one like a  throne she has fully embraced the path  ahead of her the second thing is this  giant full moon not only does it look  badass but it may also tie into the  quick shot of singed in his lab why  werewolves here we can see this  claw-like figure hanging from the  ceiling which if you compare it to the  official artwork from riot appears to be  warwick and there are several hints  throughout the season that warwick is  vander transformed when jinx  hallucinates we see this wolf-like  drawing around his body in episode 1  vander is referred to as the hound of  the underworld so you're vander  hound of the underground plus warwick's  official bio says the following though  many think of warwick as no more than a  beast buried beneath the fury lies the  mind of a man a gangster who put down  his blade and took up a new name to live  a better life but no matter how hard he  tried to move on he could never escape  the sins of the past i could definitely  see this vander warwick plotline coming  in season 2. then there's this pocket  watch singed holds inside a picture of a  girl this could be orianna who once was  a young girl but after a tragic accident  in the lower districts her body was  replaced piece by piece both characters  seem to have the same bun hairstyle and  it would make sense that singed has a  picture of her in a pocket watch  considering orianna is comprised of  clockwork speaking of clocks and time  did you notice this device in the shot  between echo and heimerdinger echo is a  character known to manipulate time  through his own invention the z drive i  wasn't sure if this was the beginnings  of that invention or part of his flying  skateboard but regardless his ability to  turn back time may be one of several  theories that saves jace mel and victor  from the rocket attack but let's say  that's not what happens there are  several juicy possibilities out there  i'm gonna list them all here and you can  decide which ones you think make the  most sense one theory is that mel  medarda is a magic user prior to the  attack she takes off her ring a ring  which can be purchased as riot  merchandise hinting that she's probably  not going anywhere and there are even  rumors she may be an upcoming champion  also right before the attack mel  experiences this sort of spider sense as  the back of her gold dress glows now  this could simply be the reflection of  the rocket but it is nighttime i'm kind  of unsure on this one let me know what  you think below then there's jace we saw  how jace was given one of these  gemstones that allowed him and his  mother to teleport when he was a child  that could be a possibility there's also  this shield he can create with his  hammer let's also not forget about  victor who is also at this meeting this  is a guy who almost killed himself this  episode it isn't far-fetched to think he  may sacrifice himself he is or at least  was dying after all he's also known to  carry shimmer in his cane and we know  that shimmer has healing properties time  travel magic shimmer and hextech are all  possible theories as to where season 2  might kick off but i want to hear your  thoughts and theories in the comments  below i friggin loved arcane and if you  did too remember to like and subscribe  so more people can see this video thanks  for watching everyone for more bad takes  you can follow me on twitter and  instagram at thinkstoryyt until next  time remember daddy loves you very much

